    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive unit at a 74.56 efficiency score. Benefiting from a favorable matchup against Houser, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees a significant boost from his SP skill rating (+19%) and platoon advantage (+14%), making him the clear catalyst for our 5x5 production. **Gunnar Henderson** follows closely with a 71.72 rating; despite facing the formidable Gilbert, **Gunnar Henderson** retains a high floor due to park factors that play significantly into his profile, effectively neutralizing the SP risk. **Nasim Nunez** provides a sneaky, high-upside play at 61.51, where his switch-hitting versatility and the weak SP xERA of 4.78 provide an ideal environment for him to exploit the bases, keeping our SB focus firmly in reach.\n\nThe bench decision process was anchored by the exclusion of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.86). While his talent is undeniable, the optimizer favored the daily efficiency of **Nolan Schanuel** (54.71) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.33) due to their platoon-favorable matchups against weaker arms. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** was ultimately benched to avoid the \"Wheeler tax,\" as the high-tier SP skill of the opponent stifled his potential output relative to the rest of the lineup. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both are squaring off against the elite arm of Skenes. Their scores are depressed by the SP skill factor (-19%), but they remain in the lineup over bench options like **Coby Mayo** (42.37) and **Dominic Smith** (35.87) because they remain essential for maintaining our desired volume across all five categories. Keep a close eye on **Liam Hicks** and **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order; their efficiency is highly dependent on early-inning success against the shaky control of Holmes.",
